    "chunk_text": "The Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n\u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba\n\n\u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2\n\n\u0d85\u0d82\u0d9a 2133/46 - 2019 \u0151\u0263 \u0db8\u0dc3 25 \u0dc0\u0dd0\u01e7 \u022f\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dca\u0db4\u01af\u01e6\u0daf\u0dcf - 2019.07.25\n\nNo. 2133/46\u2013 THURSDAY, JULY, 25, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\nANNUAL PERAHARA OF BADULL KATARAGAMA DEVALAYA\n\nIN accordance with the powers vested in me by Gazette Notifications No. 9902 of 10.09.1948, No. 10283 of 17.08.1951 and No. 14778 of 25.03.1955 published under Chapter 362 of the Pilgrimage Act, and under the powers conferred on Divisional Secretaries by Act No. 58 of 1992, and according to the constitution published in No. 1622 Gazette Notification of 02.10.2009 on Annual Perehara of Badulla Kataragama Devalaya, I Nihal Gunarathne, the Divisional Secretary of Badulla do hereby make the following orders in connection with the Annual Perehara of Badulla Katharagama Devalaya, 2018. 1. I, do hereby notice that, the Annual Perehara of Badulla Katharagana Devalaya shall begin with \u201cKap Situvima\u201d on 31st of August 2019 and by having inner Perehara from 31st August 2019 to 04th September 2019 (5 days), by having Kumbal Perehara from 05th September 2019 to 09 th September 2019 (05 days), by having Randoli Perahera from 10th September to 14th September 2019 (5 days) by having water cutting ceremony in the morning on 15th September 2019 and end in the afternoon on 15th September 2019 after having returned to the Devalaya. 2. Route of the Perehara The Perahera shall start from Badull Katharagama Devalaya premises and proceed along Badulla lower Street, Passara Road (Muthiyangana Roundabout), Longden Road, Anagarika Dharmapala Mawatha, Cocowatte Road, Udayaraja Mawatha, King\u2019s Street, Bazzar Street lower Street and back to Badulla Katharagama Devalaya. 3. Cooking and selling article of trade are prohibited in and around Badulla Katharagama Devalaya compound where the throne of the Devalaya located.\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART I : SECTION (I) \u2014 GENERAL\n\nGovernment Notifications"
