    "chunk_text": "1AIII fldgi \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2019'07'26PART III \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 26.07.2019\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%hThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nw;s \u00fafYI EXTRAORDINARY\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART III \u2013 LANDS\n\nLand Acquisition Notices\n\nwxl 2133$58 \u2013 2019 cQ,s 26 jeks isl=rdod \u2013 2019'07'26No. 2133/58 \u2013 FRIDAY, JULY 26, 2019\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nTHE LAND ACQUISITION ACT (CHAPTER 460)\n\nOrder under Proviso (a) to Section 38\n\nOrder No. 132 of 2019\n\nMy Ref No.: 4-3/9/2017/WS/ 379D.S. Ref. No. - MLB/LND/LNDAQ/L1/53\n\nBY virtue of the powers vested in me by Proviso (a) to Section 38 ofthe Land Acquisition Act (Chapter 460), I Gayantha KarunathillekeMinister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms do hereby direct theAcquiring Officer or any other officer authorised by him referred toin Paragraph 1 of the Schedule to take immediate possession of theland specified in the corresponding entry in paragraph 2 of thatSchedule.\n\nGayantha Karunatilleke, Minister of Lands & Parliamentary Reforms.\n\nMinistry of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms,\"Mihikaha Medura\",1200/6, Rajamalwatta Road,Battaramulla.11th July, 2019.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\n1. Acquiring Officer. - Divisional Secretary, Malimbada.\n\n2. Description of the Land - An allotment of land depicted in\n\nbelow name and extent in the Advance Tracing No. MR/MLM/\n\n2017/657 and dated 08.05.2018, prepared by the Survey General,\n\nsituated in the village called Katuwangoda in the Waligam Korele\n\nMinor Division in the Divisonal Secretary Division of Malimbada\n\nin Matara District in Southern Province and bounded as follows:\n\n01. Lot 'A' - Aralugaha Koratuwa - Extent: About 0.0026\n\nHectare\n\nNorth: Aralugaha Koratuwa claimed by W. A. K. Sarathchandra\n\nand Nalani Satharasingha and Road; East and South: Road; West:\n\nAralugaha Koratuwa claimed by W. A. K. Sarathchandra and Nalani\n\nSatharasingha."
